cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this talk pack, please cite it as below."
title: "A Practitioner's Guide to Knowledge Graphs — talk pack"
abstract: >-
  Companion pack for the talk "A Practitioner's Guide to Knowledge Graphs"
  (AI Engineer World's Fair 2026, Graph Track). A three-act practitioner
  narrative — bad graph to good graph to payoff — with a runnable graphtools
  library and offline-replayable notebooks covering schemaless extraction,
  schema-first curation, entity resolution, and the graph algorithms (PPR,
  HITS, shortest-path, subgraph matching) that make graphs worth it.
type: software
authors:
